          {
            title: 'FilkÃ³',
            subtitle: 'The Hungarian Master & Servant Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "FilkÃ³ is a traditional Hungarian trick-taking game popular in the Great Plain (AlfÃ¶ld) region. Closely related to the Romanian FilicÄƒu, it is a variant of the Central European Schafkopf family. The game is played with a 32ndcard Germanndsuited deck and pits two teams against each other in a battle for 'Master' status. Beyond the card play, FilkÃ³ is known for its social 'punishment' rules, where the losers (Slaves) are tasked with dealing and other minor social forfeits until they can reclaim the title of Master.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Derived from the ancient Schafkopf (Sheep's Head) game of Germany, FilkÃ³ followed the migration and trade patterns of the Austro-Hungarian Empire. While it shares many rules with other regional variants like SixtydSix, its partnership structure and 'Master/Slave' social dynamic are uniquely preserved in the Hungarian AlfÃ¶ld.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players in two partnerships (standard). 5 and 6ndplayer versions exist using modified decks.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32-card German deck. Suits: Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32-card German deck. Suits: Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Anticlockwise. 8 cards per player (in the 4ndplayer game). The dealer's bottom card determines the trump suit (excluding Over-Knaves).",
              },
            ],
          },
